    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. A viral cold with low fever. Negative rapid tests; no signs of streptococcal pharyngitis (cough, no exudate), sinusitis, or pneumonia, so no antibiotic. The cough began with the cold, so it is not the dry cough that lisinopril can cause; if a dry cough outlasts the cold, that will be reconsidered. [S]<list><item>Acetaminophen 500 to 1000 mg every 6 hours as needed, no more than 3 g a day.</item><item>Avoid decongestants (pseudoephedrine and phenylephrine), which raise blood pressure, and ibuprofen and other NSAIDs, which raise blood pressure and add bleeding risk with aspirin.</item><item>Avoid sedating antihistamines, which add to the drowsiness levetiracetam can cause; use saline nasal rinses, honey, and fluids instead.</item><item>Return or call for breathlessness, fever above 38.5 C for more than three days, or symptoms lasting beyond ten days.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy on levetiracetam (G40.209)</content>. No seizure; every dose taken. Fever and lost sleep both lower the seizure threshold. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice daily; do not skip doses while unwell.</item><item>Cancel evening events this week and sleep at least seven hours.</item><item>Seizure action plan unchanged; staff know what to do.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension on lisinopril (I10)</content>. 136/86 mmHg with a fever; above target, to be reassessed when well. [S]<list><item>Continue lisinopril 10 mg; review at next week&apos;s visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice guideline update summary: Efficacy and tolerability of the new antiepileptic drugs I: Treatment of new-onset epilepsy (2018); 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Four-week chronic-care visit next week as scheduled; sooner for the warning signs above. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-15: four-week review of levetiracetam, blood pressure, the second rhythm monitor, mood, and cognition. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
